# A ONE-CELL LANE RUNNING ALONG THE EDGE OF THE BRIDGE.
#
# Not a level -- a measurement. The maze puts its outer boundary in an explicit
# WALL column, which costs a lane; the alternative is to let the deck's own
# parapet be that boundary, since `has_wall` already railings any solid cell in
# the outermost column and WALL_HEIGHT is 2.0, exactly the height a maze wall is.
#
# THE QUESTION IS WHETHER A BODY CAN WALK THAT LANE. A parapet is a 0.3 m slab
# inset at the cell edge, and this repo has form: a flat-bottomed cylinder catches
# on the far lip of a gap, and two boxes placed face to face are that with the gap
# set to zero. So before a design change rests on it, walk it.
#
# x0 is deck the whole way, x1 is a 2-unit wall, and the entry and exit rows are
# solid across so the segment validates.

name = test_edge_lane
base_height = 0
width = 15
length = 12
tags = fixture, edge

